          "text": "{\n  \"code\": \"r0, r1, h = 18.0, 46.0, 58.0\\nseam = 0.47\\nslant = math.sqrt(h*h + (r1-r0)*(r1-r0))\\nk = (r1-r0)/slant\\nrho0, rho1 = r0/k, r1/k\\nhalf_angle = math.pi*k\\n\\n# Sample true developed coordinates at spacing below 0.114 mm.\\nx = np.linspace(-2.0, 110.0, 1001)\\ny = np.linspace(-108.0, 108.0, 1901)\\nU, V = np.meshgrid(x, y)\\nrho = np.hypot(U, V)\\nphi = np.arctan2(V, U)\\ntheta = seam + (phi + half_angle)/k\\nr = k*rho\\nZ = (rho-rho0)*h/slant\\nX = r*np.cos(theta)\\nY = r*np.sin(theta)\\n\\n# Annular sector bounded by the lower and upper rims and seam edges.\\nfield = np.minimum(rho-rho0, rho1-rho)\\nfield = np.minimum(field, U*math.sin(half_angle)-np.abs(V)*math.cos(half_angle))\\n\\n# Distance to the normalized infinite drilling axis.\\nnorm = math.sqrt(1.0 + 0.35**2 + 0.55**2)\\nnx, ny, nz = 1.0/norm, 0.35/norm, 0.55/norm\\ndx, dy, dz = X-4.0, Y-5.0, Z-29.0\\nalong = dx*nx + dy*ny + dz*nz\\ndistance = np.sqrt(np.maximum(dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz - along*along, 0.0))\\nfield = np.minimum(field, distance-14.0)\\n\\nsvg = contour_svg(x, y, field)\",\n  \"explanation\": \"The exact cone development uses slant length L = sqrt(height\u00b2 + (r1\u2212r0)\u00b2) and k = (r1\u2212r0)/L. Its developed radius is r/k, and its polar angle is k(theta\u2212seam\u2212pi), placing the lower seam on the negative-angle edge. Each developed point is mapped back to the cone and removed wherever its perpendicular distance to the normalized infinite drill axis is below 14 mm, capturing both wall crossings. The tested code exports genuine vector contours at spacing below 0.114 mm, within the 0.15 mm accuracy requirement, using the required SVG convention.\"\n}"
